Subject: [PATCH] Outbound TCP and UDP only through the injected dialer

claude-abroad (design 4.5): UDP forwarding now calls configuration.DialContext
(was a bare net.Dial that ignored the bound-interface dialer). TCP and UDP
both refuse when no dialer is configured (TCP: RST; UDP: drop) instead of
falling back to an unbound net.Dialer. Fail closed.

Note: the services mux (including /forwarder/expose) is only reachable from the
guest if the embedding program serves it on the gateway (gvproxy does, on :80);
claude-abroad never serves it, so no change is needed here.

---
--- a/pkg/services/forwarder/tcp.go
+++ b/pkg/services/forwarder/tcp.go
@@ -37,10 +37,13 @@
 			r.Complete(true)
 			return
 		}
-		dial := (&net.Dialer{}).DialContext
-		if len(dialers) > 0 && dialers[0] != nil {
-			dial = dialers[0]
+		// claude-abroad：出站只能经注入的拨号器（绑定物理网卡、失败即拒绝）；没有拨号器就拒绝，
+		// 不退回不绑定的 net.Dialer。
+		if len(dialers) == 0 || dialers[0] == nil {
+			r.Complete(true)
+			return
 		}
+		dial := dialers[0]
 		outbound, err := dial(context.Background(), "tcp", net.JoinHostPort(localAddress.String(), fmt.Sprint(r.ID().LocalPort)))
 		if err != nil {
 			log.Tracef("net.Dial() = %v", err)
